1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:03,043
Meet two partners. Ramayya invests two thousand rupees, and

2
00:00:03,043 --> 00:00:06,065
keeps that money in the business for twelve months.

3
00:00:06,065 --> 00:00:08,808
Gopalam invests three thousand rupees for nine months. At

4
00:00:08,808 --> 00:00:11,423
the end of the year the business earns a

5
00:00:11,423 --> 00:00:15,580
profit. Should the two partners share that profit equally?

6
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:19,180
No. Profit in a partnership is shared in the

7
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:21,411
ratio of what each partner contributed.

8
00:00:22,027 --> 00:00:25,716
A ratio is an ordered comparison. Three to two

9
00:00:25,716 --> 00:00:28,107
is not the same as two to three. The

10
00:00:28,107 --> 00:00:31,327
order of the two terms matters. If we swap

11
00:00:31,327 --> 00:00:33,467
the two terms of a ratio, we get its

12
00:00:33,467 --> 00:00:37,475
inverse ratio: a to b becomes b to a.

13
00:00:37,475 --> 00:00:40,127
So the inverse of four to five is five

14
00:00:40,127 --> 00:00:43,915
to four. Inverse means swap the terms. It never

15
00:00:43,915 --> 00:00:46,818
means add them, and it never means change their signs.

16
00:00:47,507 --> 00:00:49,811
Now suppose both partners keep their money in for

17
00:00:49,811 --> 00:00:52,527
the same time. Ramayya invests two thousand rupees for

18
00:00:52,527 --> 00:00:55,397
twelve months. Gopalam also invests for twelve months, but

19
00:00:55,397 --> 00:00:58,280
he puts in three thousand rupees. The time is

20
00:00:58,280 --> 00:01:01,747
the same for both, so the time factor cancels.

21
00:01:01,747 --> 00:01:05,440
The capitals are in the ratio two thousand to

22
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:08,717
three thousand, which simplifies to two to three. So

23
00:01:08,717 --> 00:01:12,538
the profit is divided in the ratio two to three.

24
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:15,242
Now suppose both partners invest the same capital. Each

25
00:01:15,242 --> 00:01:18,280
of them invests five thousand rupees. But Ramayya keeps

26
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:21,730
his money in for twelve months, while Gopalam keeps

27
00:01:21,730 --> 00:01:24,612
his in for only nine months. The capital is

28
00:01:24,612 --> 00:01:28,480
the same for both, so the capital factor cancels.

29
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:31,137
The times are in the ratio twelve to nine,

30
00:01:31,137 --> 00:01:34,380
and that simplifies to four to three. So here

31
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:37,791
the profit follows the time ratio, four to three.

32
00:01:38,353 --> 00:01:40,330
But in our business, both the money and the

33
00:01:40,330 --> 00:01:44,343
time are different. Ramayya gives two thousand rupees for

34
00:01:44,343 --> 00:01:47,378
twelve months. Gopalam gives three thousand rupees for nine

35
00:01:47,378 --> 00:01:51,400
months. The capital ratio is two to three. The

36
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:53,533
time ratio is twelve to nine, that is four

37
00:01:53,533 --> 00:01:57,253
to three. Neither ratio alone can decide the profit,

38
00:01:57,253 --> 00:01:59,624
so the two ratios must be combined.

39
00:02:00,347 --> 00:02:02,935
To combine two ratios we use the compound ratio.

40
00:02:02,935 --> 00:02:05,267
For the ratios a to b and c to

41
00:02:05,267 --> 00:02:08,897
d, multiply the first terms together, and multiply the

42
00:02:08,897 --> 00:02:12,632
second terms together. The compound ratio is a times

43
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:16,467
c to b times d. A common mistake is

44
00:02:16,467 --> 00:02:19,027
to add the terms instead, and write a plus

45
00:02:19,027 --> 00:02:21,571
c to b plus d. That is wrong. A

46
00:02:21,571 --> 00:02:25,578
compound ratio multiplies corresponding terms; it never adds them.

47
00:02:26,213 --> 00:02:30,313
Let us apply the rule. We multiply the capital

48
00:02:30,313 --> 00:02:33,833
ratio two to three by the time ratio four

49
00:02:33,833 --> 00:02:36,189
to three. Two times four is eight, and three

50
00:02:36,189 --> 00:02:39,393
times three is nine, so the compound ratio is

51
00:02:39,393 --> 00:02:42,878
eight to nine. Let us cross-check with money multiplied

52
00:02:42,878 --> 00:02:45,896
by time. Two thousand times twelve is twenty four

53
00:02:45,896 --> 00:02:48,713
thousand, and three thousand times nine is twenty seven

54
00:02:48,713 --> 00:02:53,530
thousand. Twenty four thousand to twenty seven thousand simplifies

55
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:56,864
to eight to nine, so the compound ratio is correct.

56
00:02:57,460 --> 00:03:00,080
Now let us turn that ratio into rupees. Suppose

57
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:03,060
the profit for the year is seventeen thousand rupees.

58
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:06,620
This total is an example, not a textbook figure.

59
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:09,535
The ratio is eight to nine, so the profit

60
00:03:09,535 --> 00:03:12,620
is divided into eight plus nine, that is seventeen,

61
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:17,090
equal parts. Seventeen thousand divided by seventeen gives one

62
00:03:17,090 --> 00:03:19,753
thousand rupees for each part. Ramayya takes eight parts,

63
00:03:19,753 --> 00:03:23,093
that is eight thousand rupees. Gopalam takes nine parts,

64
00:03:23,093 --> 00:03:26,522
that is nine thousand rupees, and eight thousand plus

65
00:03:26,522 --> 00:03:30,651
nine thousand is seventeen thousand. The whole profit is shared.

66
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:34,057
Here is the decision rule to remember. If the

67
00:03:34,057 --> 00:03:35,541
time is the same, share the profit in the

68
00:03:35,541 --> 00:03:39,300
ratio of the capitals. If the capital is the

69
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:42,496
same, share it in the ratio of the times.

70
00:03:42,496 --> 00:03:44,991
If both the capital and the time are different,

71
00:03:44,991 --> 00:03:48,225
share it in the compound ratio of capital and

72
00:03:48,225 --> 00:03:50,128
time. So the share of the profit follows capital

73
00:03:50,128 --> 00:03:51,251
multiplied by time.

74
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:55,876
Your turn. Four quick checks. First: write the inverse

75
00:03:55,876 --> 00:03:59,640
of the ratio seven to five. Second: find the

76
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:02,044
compound ratio of three to four and two to

77
00:04:02,044 --> 00:04:06,320
three. Third: compound three to four with the inverse

78
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:10,800
of four to five. And last: partner P invests

79
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:13,730
four thousand rupees for six months, and partner Q

80
00:04:13,730 --> 00:04:16,987
invests three thousand rupees for eight months. In what

81
00:04:16,987 --> 00:04:18,891
ratio should they share the profit?

82
00:04:29,787 --> 00:04:31,197
The inverse of seven to five is five to

83
00:04:31,197 --> 00:04:33,581
seven, because the inverse swaps the two terms. The

84
00:04:33,581 --> 00:04:36,172
compound ratio of three to four and two to

85
00:04:36,172 --> 00:04:38,023
three is six to twelve, which simplifies to one

86
00:04:38,023 --> 00:04:41,793
to two. Three to four, compounded with the inverse

87
00:04:41,793 --> 00:04:43,847
of four to five, is three times five to

88
00:04:43,847 --> 00:04:46,067
four times four, that is fifteen to sixteen. And

89
00:04:46,067 --> 00:04:50,818
for P and Q, four thousand times six is

90
00:04:50,818 --> 00:04:53,900
twenty four thousand, and three thousand times eight is

91
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:56,625
also twenty four thousand. So the ratio is one

92
00:04:56,625 --> 00:05:00,078
to one, and the two partners share the profit equally.

93
00:05:00,693 --> 00:05:03,351
One last look. The inverse ratio swaps the two

94
00:05:03,351 --> 00:05:07,608
terms: a to b becomes b to a. The

95
00:05:07,608 --> 00:05:10,933
compound ratio multiplies corresponding terms: a to b and

96
00:05:10,933 --> 00:05:13,330
c to d give a times c to b

97
00:05:13,330 --> 00:05:17,065
times d. In a partnership, a partner's share follows

98
00:05:17,065 --> 00:05:19,953
capital multiplied by time. And when the profit is

99
00:05:19,953 --> 00:05:23,353
known, divide it into equal parts using the ratio.

100
00:05:23,353 --> 00:05:26,217
Money and time together decide the share. Thank you

101
00:05:26,217 --> 00:05:29,684
for watching, and see you in the next lesson.
